$NetBSD$

Replace only the .ec suffix when mkerr.pl derives the state file name.
The unescaped pattern also matched an earlier "ec" with any character
before it in a directory name, such as a hash, so the build could not
open the error configuration file.
Origin: EmberBSD (AI-assisted); upstream status: not submitted.

--- util/mkerr.pl.orig
+++ util/mkerr.pl
@@ -196,7 +196,7 @@
 
 if ( ! $statefile ) {
     $statefile = $config;
-    $statefile =~ s/.ec/.txt/;
+    $statefile =~ s/\.ec$/.txt/;
 }
 
 # Unless a rewrite or a report was explicitly requested, skip the run
